      "side": 1,
      "message": "usleep(4) when t0 is sampled right before a tick. In this case, the timer may immediately tick + 4us, and may tick +4us again 3.8us later (not 4us later). So we\u0027ll end our delay at t \u003d 3.8us, despite being asked to delay 4us. It can get slightly worse even with something like usleep(12), if we get consecutive 4us ticks (remember that the counter ticks in a cycle something like (4us, 4us, 4us, 4us, 3us, ... ). We can end our delay at t \u003d 11.4us.\n\nAnyway thinking about this more, we\u0027re likely to have .6us of overhead, so I will reduce this to ticks_to_usecs(1) + 1 (that\u0027s a constant 4 us).",
